{
  "_about": "Component spec for pos-radio (docs/inspect refactor, component migration batch, 2026-08-26). Single source of truth for the Variants/Usage/Tokens tabs on /style-guide \"Radio\" section. Reuses the already-curated usage prose from COMP_CONFIGS['radio'].usage and token data from COMP_CONFIGS['radio'].tokens (verified-accurate, currently-live data) restructured into the new schema. Single representative variant — this component's preview shows one instance (no Variant/Base toggle needed per the 2026-08-25/26 \"multiple sub-variants side by side\" rule). Regenerate the spec partial with the script in RULES.md 6.4 if the source data changes; do not hand-edit token values here. Updated 2026-08-27: added usageExample/props/composedOf (Target architecture point 1 fields that were left empty when this spec was first generated). Disabled checked fill/frame borrows the primary button disabled tokens (--pos-color-button-primary-disabled-background / -frame) — documented exception to RULES.md 2.2, see COMPONENT-RULES.md.",
  "component": "radio",
  "name": "Radio",
  "description": "Selecting exactly one option from a set of mutually exclusive choices.",
  "whenToUse": [
    "Selecting exactly one option from a set of mutually exclusive choices.",
    "The user must make a choice — all options should be visible upfront."
  ],
  "whenNotToUse": [
    "Multiple selections are valid — use checkboxes instead.",
    "There are more than ~6 options — consider a <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> dropdown instead.",
    "There is only one option — use a checkbox or switch instead."
  ],
  "do": [
    "Group all related radio inputs under the same <code>name</code> attribute so only one can be selected at a time.",
    "Wrap each input+label pair in a <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code> with a <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code> describing the group.",
    "Pre-select the most common or safe default option with the <code>checked</code> attribute."
  ],
  "dont": [
    "Use a radio group for binary yes/no — a checkbox or toggle is clearer.",
    "Leave the group with no default selection unless the user must actively choose."
  ],
  "accessibility": [
    "All radio inputs in a group must share the same <code>name</code> — this is how the browser enforces mutual exclusion and announces the group to screen readers.",
    "Each input must have a <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> associated via matching <code>for</code> and <code>id</code>.",
    "Wrap the group in a <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code> with a <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code> so assistive technology announces the group label before each option."
  ],
  "composedOf": [],
  "props": [
    {
      "name": "name",
      "type": "attribute",
      "default": "required",
      "description": "All radios in a group must share the same name attribute — enforces mutual exclusion."
    },
